// 5:3, five equal bars of 0.6.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Singleish Pride Flag"
  designer "NonMonoPrideFlags (DeviantArt)"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  date "2016-06-21"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20220127054530/https://www.deviantart.com/nonmonoprideflags/art/Singleish-Pride-Flag-616698330"
  note "NonMonoPrideFlags's DeviantArt post 'Singleish Pride Flag', as the Wayback Machine held it on 27 January 2022, says: 'This is my pride flag design for singleish relationships', a non-monogamous attitude of someone not in a primary relationship who dates several people at once, openly and with no expectation of long-term commitment. It gives no color meanings, measurements or color values. The post is dated 21 June 2016 (UTC)."
  note "The post's image, the original file, is a JPEG of 541 by 330 pixels, 1.64:1, the size of the designer's earlier flags, so no deliberate proportion is clear. This file uses the common 5:3. The image draws five equal bars, of 65 or 66 pixels each."
  note "The colors are read from the image's pixels, which are flat in the bars: purple #70397d, cyan #a5ffff and grey #7d7a8d."
}
palette {
  purple "#70397d"
  cyan "#a5ffff"
  grey "#7d7a8d"
}
proportion hoist=3 fly=5

bars purple cyan grey cyan purple
